TA-ups
====

Collects UPS health from Network UPS Tools (upsc) or apcupsd (apcaccess) when a UPS server is reachable: device model, online/off-battery status, battery charge, load and input voltage list. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype ups:status) and ups.* metrics (device count, battery charge, on-battery flag) to index=metrics (sourcetype ups:metrics); hosts without a UPS server report 'absent'.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * Optional: nut-client (upsc) with a NUT server, or apcupsd/apcaccess; auto-detected
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="ups:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="ups:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="ups.*" by host
  | mstats avg("ups.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=ups:status  (per-device JSON: model, status, charge, load, voltage)
Metrics: ups.device_count, ups.<dev>_charge, ups.<dev>_on_battery
Alarm status when any UPS is on battery (OLB).
Dashboards: TA-Ups > Ups Overview / Ups Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-ups/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * upsc needs the NUT server running and reachable from the monitored host.
  * No UPS present => status 'absent', ups.device_count=0 (not an alarm).

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-ups).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-ups/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
